IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-art01-commencement`

-- je54-tests-art01-commencement: Article 1, for a TEXT of the Law passed in by hand (the date-to-text step is tested in je54-tests-vintage and je54-tests-art01-by-date).
-- The expected values were written from the text of Articles 1(1) to 1(7) before this module was run.  Jersey local time is UTC+0 in winter and UTC+1 (BST) in summer; the tz database zone is
-- Europe/Jersey, and the zone is an input (assumed, not ruled: the Law names none).  In 2020 the clocks went forward on 29 March, so 00:00 on 1 April 2020 in Jersey is 23:00 UTC on 31 March.

`text V1` MEANS `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021`
`text V2a` MEANS `V2a, 28 September 2021 to 30 January 2022`
`text V2b` MEANS `V2b, 31 January 2022 to 31 August 2022`
`text V2c` MEANS `V2c, 1 September 2022 to 10 January 2024`
`text V2d` MEANS `V2d, 11 January 2024 to 23 November 2025`
`text V2e` MEANS `V2e, 24 November 2025 to 18 June 2026`
`text V2f` MEANS `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current`
`text inferred` MEANS `the inferred text from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018`
`text none` MEANS `no text before 28 March 2003`

GIVEN named IS A DATE
      made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that names the day` named `and was made on` made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `on a particular day`
        `the day it names` IS JUST named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `forthwith`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that is silent, made on` made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that counts from its promulgation, made on` made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `calculated by reference to its promulgation`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that says a particular day but names none, made on` made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `on a particular day`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`an instant in UTC` y mo d h mi s MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD y mo d) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mi s) "Etc/UTC"

§ `Articles 1(5) and 1(6): a named day (the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021)`

§§ `The day, and the basis`

-- Made 1 March 2020, names 1 April 2020: it comes into operation immediately on the expiration of 31 March, that is on 1 April.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2020 4 1
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the basis` EQUALS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
-- A named day before the day it was made: the Article does not care (nothing in it forbids it); the named day governs.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 2 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2020 2 1

§§ `The moment: the start of the named day, in the zone given`

-- 1 April 2020 00:00 in Jersey (BST, UTC+1) is 31 March 23:00 UTC.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 23 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 22 59 59) "Europe/Jersey" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the answer`
-- The same enactment read in the zone UTC starts one hour later: 31 March 23:00 UTC is before 1 April 00:00 UTC.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 23 0 0) "Etc/UTC" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 4 1 0 0 0) "Etc/UTC" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the answer`
-- Winter: Jersey time is UTC+0, so 15 January 2020 00:00 Jersey is 15 January 00:00 UTC.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 1 14 23 59 59) "Europe/Jersey" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 1 15) `and was made on` (YMD 2019 12 1)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 1 15 0 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 1 15) `and was made on` (YMD 2019 12 1)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the commencement of the enactment, the moment at which it comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 1 15) `and was made on` (YMD 2019 12 1)) "Europe/Jersey")'s `the basis` EQUALS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`

§§ `In force on a day: both sides of the named day`

#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2020 3 31) `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2020 4 1) `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2020 4 2) `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)))'s `the answer`

§§ `The named day is missing`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that says a particular day but names none, made on` (YMD 2020 3 1))
        BECAUSE "the enactment is said to come into operation on a particular day, but no day is named"

§ `Article 1(6): forthwith, and silent (the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021)`

-- FINDING F1.  Made on 10 June 2020 and saying forthwith (or silent), the enactment is construed as expressed to come into operation on 10 June, and then Article 1(5) applies: it comes into operation at the start of 10 June.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10)))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2020 6 10
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10)))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2020 6 10
-- 10 June 2020 00:00 in Jersey (BST) is 9 June 23:00 UTC: the enactment is in force an hour before the day was even a day in Jersey, and well before it was made.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 6 9 23 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 6 9 22 59 59) "Europe/Jersey" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10)))'s `the answer`
-- Made at 15:00 on 10 June (14:00 UTC) and asked about at 08:00 Jersey time (07:00 UTC) that morning: already in force, before it was made.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 6 10 7 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2020 6 9) `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10)))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2020 6 10) `under` `text V1` (`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10)))'s `the answer`

§ `Articles 1(5) and 1(6): a time calculated from promulgation is not given a day`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V1` (`an enactment that counts from its promulgation, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10))
        BECAUSE "the time is calculated by reference to promulgation: Article 1(7) fixes the date of promulgation when it is unknown, but neither Law says how a period is counted from it, so no day is given"

§ `Articles 1(5) and 1(6): the days from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018 (inferred) and before`

-- Inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation: the same rule, labelled.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text inferred` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `and was made on` (YMD 2014 9 1)))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2014 11 21
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text inferred` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `and was made on` (YMD 2014 9 1)))'s `the basis` EQUALS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text inferred` (`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` (YMD 2010 5 5)))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2010 5 5
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2014 11 21) `under` `text inferred` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `and was made on` (YMD 2014 9 1)))'s `the basis` EQUALS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2014 11 20) `under` `text inferred` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `and was made on` (YMD 2014 9 1)))'s `the answer`
-- Before 28 March 2003 even Articles 1(5) and 1(6) refuse.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text none` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 1990 1 1) `and was made on` (YMD 1989 6 1))
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019); and before 28 March 2003 the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation do not date Article 1(5) or 1(6) either (L.16/2003 amended 1(5) and inserted 1(6) on that day)"

§ `Articles 1(5) and 1(6): from 28 September 2021 they are deleted, and the rule is the 2021 Law's`

-- Each of the six later texts answers the same: a refusal that names the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3.  The row does not borrow the 2021 Law's rule.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V2a` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 15) `and was made on` (YMD 2021 9 30))
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V2b` (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2022 2 1))
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V2c` (`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` (YMD 2023 1 1))
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V2d` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2025 1 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2024 6 1))
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V2e` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2025 12 1))
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` `text V2f` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2026 10 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2026 9 1))
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(4): the commencement of the enactment, the moment at which it comes into operation` `text V2f` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2026 10 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2026 9 1)) "Europe/Jersey"
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` (YMD 2026 10 2) `under` `text V2f` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2026 10 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2026 9 1))
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

§ `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation when it is unknown`

-- Known: the known date is used.  Unknown: the day the enactment was passed or made.  All seven deposited texts say the same.
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V1` TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 5 5)) (YMD 2020 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 5 5
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V1` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2020 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 5 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V2a` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2021 10 1) EQUALS YMD 2021 10 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V2b` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2022 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2022 2 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V2c` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2023 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2023 2 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V2d` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2024 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V2e` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2025 12 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V2f` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 1
-- The Article applies only where the time is expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text V1` FALSE NOTHING (YMD 2020 5 1)
        BECAUSE "Article 1(7) deals only with a time at which an enactment is to come into operation that is expressed or calculated by reference to its promulgation"
-- Not among the four provisions answered before 1 January 2019.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text inferred` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2010 5 1)
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` `text none` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 1990 5 1)
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 1(1): what an enactment is`

#ASSERT `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V1` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V1` `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of an Order in Council` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V2c` `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V2d` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V2f` `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of an Order in Council` FALSE
-- "shall mean": something that is none of these is not an enactment.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V1` `something that is none of these` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V2f` `something that is none of these` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text V1` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 1(1) does not say what enactment then means"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text inferred` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` `text none` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 1(2): when a Law is deemed passed (the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021)`

-- Reading taken (I3): the later of the day it was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and the day it was registered by the Royal Court.
#ASSERT `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 3 15
#ASSERT `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 20) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 3 20
#ASSERT `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 3 15
-- The stated day is ignored on reading 1.
#ASSERT `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` (JUST (YMD 2020 4 4)) FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 3 15
-- Reading 2: the caller states the day, which must not be earlier than the later of the two.
#ASSERT `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Article only bars an earlier day: the caller states the day` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 15)) FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 3 15
#ASSERT `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Article only bars an earlier day: the caller states the day` (JUST (YMD 2020 4 4)) FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 4 4
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Article only bars an earlier day: the caller states the day` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 14)) FALSE
        BECAUSE "the day stated is earlier than the later of the day the Law was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and the day it was registered by the Royal Court: Article 1(2) says a Law is not deemed passed until both"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Article only bars an earlier day: the caller states the day` NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "on the reading that Article 1(2) only bars an earlier day, the Article fixes no day: the caller must state the day on which the Law is deemed passed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V1` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 1(2) does not say when a Law is deemed passed"
-- Deleted from 28 September 2021; not among the provisions answered before 1 January 2019.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V2a` (YMD 2021 10 1) (YMD 2021 10 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 1(2) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not among the provisions answered before 1 January 2019"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text V2f` (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 1(2) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not among the provisions answered before 1 January 2019"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `text inferred` (YMD 2010 3 1) (YMD 2010 3 15) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 1(3): passing and repeal`

#ASSERT `the reading of a reference to passing or repeal under Article 1(3)` `passing` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the making of the enactment`
#ASSERT `the reading of a reference to passing or repeal under Article 1(3)` `repeal` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the rescission of the enactment`
#ASSERT `the reading of a reference to passing or repeal under Article 1(3)` `passing` FALSE EQUALS `as written`
#ASSERT `Article 1(3): how a reference to passing or repeal is read` `text V1` `repeal` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the rescission of the enactment`
#ASSERT `Article 1(3): how a reference to passing or repeal is read` `text V2f` `passing` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the making of the enactment`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(3): how a reference to passing or repeal is read` `text inferred` `passing` TRUE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
